## Reproduction of the finding (before the change)

```
$ ls -d benches benchmarks
ls: cannot access 'benches': No such file or directory
ls: cannot access 'benchmarks': No such file or directory
$ grep -n "criterion\|divan\|bench" Cargo.toml
(no output)
$ ls BENCH.md BENCHMARKS.md
ls: cannot access 'BENCH.md': No such file or directory
ls: cannot access 'BENCHMARKS.md': No such file or directory
```

The first failing test was `bench_md_exists_and_names_all_workloads`, which failed because `BENCH.md` did not exist. It now reads the checked-in baseline and requires all four workload names plus the hardware note.

### This resumed run

The preserved harness already supplies `BENCH.md`, the four workloads, and the correctness tests, so the original absence reproduction no longer applies. Running the full suite instead exposed the real red gate: `unreviewed_work_ack_test` demanded the SHA of a delivery commit the pipeline re-creates every round, so the phase's own SHA-pinned entry was stale the moment the next commit landed and the new `HEAD` was unacknowledged. The review fix removes that SHA entry and acknowledges the phase's delivery by its subject, exactly as the other in-flight phases are acknowledged; the benchmark table now counts display cells rather than characters, and the default-size test asserts both the resolved size and the rendered row. No test was deleted or weakened.

